# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the React + Vite project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package version ^1.4.1
- Used npm as the project's package manager

### 2. Code Integration
**Modified:** `src/App.jsx`
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the main App component, placed after the Router to ensure it tracks all page views across all routes

### 3. Updated Files
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `src/App.jsx` - Integrated Analytics component

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component was placed inside the main App div, after the Router component. This ensures:
- Analytics tracks all routes (/. /electives, /contact-us)
- The component is initialized once when the app loads
- Page views are automatically tracked as users navigate between routes

## Verification

✅ **Linter:** Passed with no errors
✅ **Build:** Successfully compiled (975ms build time)
✅ **Tests:** No test suite configured (no issues)

## Next Steps

To enable analytics data collection:
1. Deploy this application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics)
3. Once deployed, verify the implementation by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

## Framework-Specific Notes

- This implementation follows React-specific instructions from Vercel docs
- The `@vercel/analytics/react` import provides the React component
- The Analytics component is a zero-config drop-in that automatically handles page view tracking
